  "broader": "https://granitestate.github.io/rules/ph/2003",
  "definition": "License Required",
  "effectiveDate": "2020-10-15",
  "historyNote": "#12336, eff 7-22-17; ss by #13117, eff 10-15-20",
  "inScheme": "https://granitestate.github.io/rules/scheme",
  "notation": "Ph 2003.02",
  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ph100-2600.html",
  "prefLabel": "Ph 2003.02 License Required",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ph 2003.02 License Required.\n\n(a) No person shall compound legend drugs or controlled drugs, as defined in RSA 318-B:1, VI, and no person acting as or employed by an outsourcing facility shall supply such drugs, without first having obtained a license from the board. No license shall be issued or renewed for an outsourcing facility unless the same shall be operated in a manner prescribed by law and according to Ph 2000. The license shall expire biennially on June 30 of each odd-numbered year. The license shall not be transferable.\n\n(b) Separate licenses shall be required for each compounding site owned or operated by an outsourcing facility. Provided, however, that an agent or employee of any licensed outsourcing facility shall not be required to be licensed under this section and may lawfully possess sterile compounded products if he or she is acting in the usual course of his or her business or employment.\n\n(c) Renewal applications shall be filed no later than June 15th of every odd-numbered year and may be obtained from the board office. Alternatively, renewal applications may be filed online at https://nhlicenses.nh.gov/eGov/Login.aspx .\n\n(d) The prescribed fee for original and biennial renewal licenses for outsourcing facilities shall be $500.00.\n\nSource. #12336, eff 7-22-17; ss by #13117, eff 10-15-20",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ph100-2600.html"
}
